   522	    def _compute_conditioning(self, metadata):
   523	        """Dispatch conditioning by cond_method (exp_03 plan §2c).
   524	
   525	        ``fa_invariant`` routes through the Route-1 yaw-symmetrized path
   526	        (cylindrical pose features + C4 frame average of the ViT conditioners);
   527	        ``fa_cartesian`` (exp_21) applies ONE mechanism to both sub-paths instead,
   528	        frame-averaging all four pose/geometry conditioners over the same orbit
   529	        with the poses left as raw Cartesian xyz; ``vanilla`` is the unchanged
   530	        single conditioner pass. Called from training_step, validation_step AND
   531	        test_step so all inference/training sites share one dispatch point (the
   532	        repo's flow_source precedent). The raise is a backstop; the constructor
   533	        already rejects unknown values.
   534	
   535	        ``max_fwd_samples`` is passed as a KEYWORD. In the ``fa_invariant`` branch
   536	        that is a slip guard — the parameter after ``angles`` is ``vit_ids``, so a
   537	        positional fifth argument would disable the frame average instead of
   538	        changing the chunk plan. In the ``fa_cartesian`` branch it is PARITY:
   539	        ``fa_cartesian_conditioning`` has no ``vit_ids`` parameter, its fifth
   540	        positional IS ``max_fwd_samples``, so the keyword buys API discipline
   541	        rather than safety. The two branches are kept in the same shape
   542	        deliberately — the arms differ in which function is called and in nothing
   543	        about how it is called.
   544	
   545	        The no-cap case takes a SEPARATE branch that issues the original
   546	        four-argument call verbatim (r1 review finding 1). ``max_fwd_samples=None``
