worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_analysis.md:34:- **For the equivariance agenda:** if the target property is yaw-robustness, finer orbits (C16+) achieve it essentially perfectly and transfer across eval orbits — at a θ=0 acoustic cost that is real but bounded (≤ ~+0.9 T60). If the target is θ=0 leaderboard accuracy under this training recipe, vanilla currently wins; the interesting open question is whether mechanism (1) recovers the legacy-recipe fa advantage at scale.
