worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_results.md:5:## R1 (primary): does a finer frame-averaging orbit beat C4? — **NO**
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_results.md:7:5-seed paired deltas vs C4L at 40k, K=8 (mean ± 95% paired-t CI, df=4; positive = worse on ↓-metrics):
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_results.md:15:Both co-primary families resolve cleanly: the K8 T60 degradation is significant for every arm (Holm-corrected within arm); K8 R@1 is null everywhere. The trend is **non-monotone** — an inverted-U peaking at C16 (adjacent-orbit deltas: C8−C4L +0.299, C16−C8 +0.630, C32−C16 −0.197 T60) — so this is not simple "more averaging = more damage" saturation. Absolute rows live in `model_comparison.md` (all four arms, both K, batched-era fa eval).
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_results.md:17:**Bridge:** C4L (this recipe) vs historical legacy-loop C4 at 40k: T60 +0.212 (K8) — the recipe/execution bridge is material, which is why all R1 comparisons are within-recipe against C4L only.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_results.md:19:## q9: frame averaging vs vanilla under the *same* recipe — **REVERSED**
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_results.md:21:VANL (vanilla, exact exp_11 recipe, one pin, single delta = frame averaging on/off), 40k, 5 seeds:
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_results.md:26:Under the legacy 2-GPU recipe, fa beat vanilla (exp_07 single-delta; exp_10 A4 fair grid 6/0 best-of). Under the L40 / 8×8 / SyncBN-64 / grad-ckpt / batched-orbit recipe, vanilla wins the acoustic parameters decisively. **The fa advantage is recipe-contingent, not intrinsic.**
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_results.md:30:Delta vs own 0° reference (s42, K8, 40k): every in-group rotation sits at the invariance floor for every arm (|ΔT60| ≤ 0.001, |ΔEDT| ≤ 0.011). Off-group residuals shrink ~an order of magnitude per refinement: C4L rot45 T60 +1.334 / EDT +3.234 / R@1 −1.231; C8 worst off-group T60 +0.104; C16 and C32 flat at every tested offset (|ΔT60| ≤ 0.026). Claim scope: tested offsets {5.625°, 11.25°, 22.5°, 45°}.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_results.md:34:Decomposition `Cn/aₙ − C4L/a₄ = eval + train + interaction` (s42, K8, 40k; full off-diagonal sets validated):
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_11_fa_orbit_claude/fa_orbit_results.md:42:(EDT concordant and larger: train +2.50/+4.66/+3.12.) The training-side term dominates and carries the inverted-U. The eval-side term is constant in n — evaluating the C4-trained model under ANY finer orbit costs ~+0.45 T60 / ~1.0 EDT / ~−0.45 R@1, saturating already at a8 — and the **legacy exp_07 B-F checkpoint replicates it era-clean** (+0.490/+0.481/+0.482 vs its own batched-era a4 baseline, same pin).
